    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nInterested in this property? Sign up for mySherryFitz to arrange your viewing, see current offers, or make your own offer. Register now at SherryFitz.ie.\n\nWelcome to Stadalt, Stamullen, Co. Meath A Home of Space, Light, and Country Charm\n\nSet back on a wonderfully private site of approximately 0.3 acres, Stadalt is a spacious four-bedroom detached family home that perfectly balances rural tranquility with everyday convenience. From the moment you arrive, the generous driveway offers ample secure parking, while the side access leads you to a surprisingly large rear garden that backs directly onto open farmland—rewarding you with uninterrupted countryside views that stretch for miles.\nInside, the home is presented in wonderful condition throughout. Two large, bright reception rooms provide versatile space for both quiet family evenings and more formal entertaining, each filled with natural light. All four bedrooms are generously proportioned, with built-in storage thoughtfully provided in each, ensuring both comfort and practicality. The property benefits from oil-fired central heating and double-glazed PVC windows, offering warmth and efficiency year-round. For those with hobbies, a home business, or simply a need for extra storage, the detached steel workshop and shed comes complete with power—an ideal space for a classic car, workshop, or garden store.\nLocation is where Stadalt truly excels. Just minutes' walk brings you into Stamullen village, while a short drive takes you to Gormanston Beach for coastal walks and its mainline railway station for easy commuting. Dublin Airport is approximately 20 minutes by car, making this an unrivalled choice for those seeking countryside serenity without sacrificing connectivity. Stadalt isn't just a house—it's a place to put down roots, breathe deeply, and enjoy the very best of County Meath living"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHall - 1.97m x 5.16m\npinewood flooring\n\nGuest w.c. - 1.97m x 1.48m\nwc, whb\n\nLiving Room - 5.81m x 3.49m\nwith large window to the front, pinewood flooring, feature marble fireplace with open fire\n\n4th Bedroom - 3.11m x 4.05m\nwith wood flooring and large window to the front\n\nInner Hallway - 1.26m x 1.93m\naccess to utility room\n\nUtility Room - 1.75m x 2.07m\nwith tiled flooring, plumbed for wahsing maching and dryer, door to side\n\nKitchen - 4.91m x 3.64m\nwith country style kitchen units with built in hob and oven, wood flooring\n\nDining Area - 4.15m x 3.64m\nwith wood burning stove and french door to rear patio area\n\nBedroom One - 3.95m x 2.94m\nwith wood flooring, walk in wardrobe with eave store room, large window to rear\n\nBedroom Two - 3.06m x 4.22m\nwith wood flooring, walk in storage room and built in wardrobes\n\nBedroom Three - 3.25m x 3.06m\nwith wood flooring, built in wardrobes\n\nBathroom - 1.75m x 2.95m\nfully tiled with wc, whb and bath with shower over.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Large detached family home, 4 Bedroom, set on c.0.3 acre private site</li><li>2 large bright reception rooms</li><li>Solar panels which heat the hot water. </li><li>All large bedrooms with storage </li><li>Wonderful condition throughout</li><li>Oil heating and double glazed PVC windows</li><li>Detached steel workshop/shed with power</li><li>Side driveway to rear garden </li><li>Backing on to farmland with excellent countryside views</li><li>Large private site with ample secure parking to the front and rear </li><li>Minutes' walk to stamullen village and short drive to Gormanston Beach, mainline railway station</li><li>c.20 minutes' drive to Dublin Airport</ul>"
      },
